  "lineage": "Dance-songs of the Wodaabe, nomadic Fulɓe cattle herders of Niger, performed at the worso gatherings that close the rainy season, when lines of young men with painted faces sing and dance the yaake and the geerewol to be judged by women; the ruume circle dance belongs to the same repertoire. Sandrine Loncke's recordings and study document its multipart singing.",
